  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor VAT-registered exporters, this means that they can effectively reduce their tax burden by recovering the input VAT on their purchases. To claim this refund or credit, exporters must ensure they comply with the necessary documentation and filing requirements as stipulated by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). This process enhances cash flow and supports the competitiveness of exporters in the global market.",
